('crossbow-light', 'Crossbow, light', 'Weapon', '25 gp', '5 lb', '1d8 (Piercing)\nPropiedades:\nAmmunition\nLoading\nTwo-Handed', NULL, 'Ammunition\nLoading\nTwo-Handed', NULL),
('crowbar', 'Crowbar', 'Adventuring Gear', '2 gp', '5 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Using a crowbar grants advantage to Strength checks where the crowbar''s leverage can be applied.'),
('crystal', 'Crystal', 'Adventuring Gear', '10 gp', '1 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'An arcane focus is a special item--an orb, a crystal, a rod, a specially constructed staff, a wand-like length of wood, or some similar item--designed to channel the power of arcane spells. A sorcerer, warlock, or wizard can use such an item as a spellcasting focus.'),
('dagger', 'Dagger', 'Weapon', '2 gp', '1 lb', '1d4 (Piercing)\nPropiedades:\nFinesse\nLight\nThrown\nMonk', NULL, 'Finesse\nLight\nThrown\nMonk', NULL),
('dart', 'Dart', 'Weapon', '5 cp', '0.25 lb', '1d4 (Piercing)\nPropiedades:\nFinesse\nThrown', NULL, 'Finesse\nThrown', NULL),
('dice-set', 'Dice Set', 'Tools', '1 sp', '0 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This item encompasses a wide range of game pieces, including dice and decks of cards (for games such as Three-Dragon Ante). A few common examples appear on the Tools table, but other kinds of gaming sets exist. If you are proficient with a gaming set, you can add your proficiency bonus to ability checks you make to play a game with that set. Each type of gaming set requires a separate proficiency.'),
('diplomats-pack', 'Diplomat''s Pack', 'Adventuring Gear', '39 gp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('disguise-kit', 'Disguise Kit', 'Adventuring Gear', '25 gp', '3 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This pouch of cosmetics, hair dye, and small props lets you create disguises that change your physical appearance. Proficiency with this kit lets you add your proficiency bonus to any ability checks you make to create a visual disguise.'),
('donkey', 'Donkey', 'Mounts and Vehicles', '8 gp', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('drum', 'Drum', 'Tools', '6 gp', '3 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Several of the most common types of musical instruments are shown on the table as examples. If you have proficiency with a given musical instrument, you can add your proficiency bonus to any ability checks you make to play music with the instrument. A bard can use a musical instrument as a spellcasting focus. Each type of musical instrument requires a separate proficiency.'),
('dulcimer', 'Dulcimer', 'Tools', '25 gp', '10 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Several of the most common types of musical instruments are shown on the table as examples. If you have proficiency with a given musical instrument, you can add your proficiency bonus to any ability checks you make to play music with the instrument. A bard can use a musical instrument as a spellcasting focus. Each type of musical instrument requires a separate proficiency.'),
