('fishing-tackle', 'Fishing tackle', 'Adventuring Gear', '1 gp', '4 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This kit includes a wooden rod, silken line, corkwood bobbers, steel hooks, lead sinkers, velvet lures, and narrow netting.'),
('flail', 'Flail', 'Weapon', '10 gp', '2 lb', '1d8 (Bludgeoning)', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('flask-or-tankard', 'Flask or tankard', 'Adventuring Gear', '2 cp', '1 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('flute', 'Flute', 'Tools', '2 gp', '1 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Several of the most common types of musical instruments are shown on the table as examples. If you have proficiency with a given musical instrument, you can add your proficiency bonus to any ability checks you make to play music with the instrument. A bard can use a musical instrument as a spellcasting focus. Each type of musical instrument requires a separate proficiency.'),
('forgery-kit', 'Forgery Kit', 'Adventuring Gear', '15 gp', '5 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This small box contains a variety of papers and parchments, pens and inks, seals and sealing wax, gold and silver leaf, and other supplies necessary to create convincing forgeries of physical documents. Proficiency with this kit lets you add your proficiency bonus to any ability checks you make to create a physical forgery of a document.'),
