('tent-two-person', 'Tent, two-person', 'Adventuring Gear', '2 gp', '20 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A simple and portable canvas shelter, a tent sleeps two.'),
('thieves-tools', 'Thieves'' Tools', 'Tools', '25 gp', '1 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This set of tools includes a small file, a set of lock picks, a small mirror mounted on a metal handle, a set of narrow-bladed scissors, and a pair of pliers. Proficiency with these tools lets you add your proficiency bonus to any ability checks you make to disarm traps or open locks.'),
('tinderbox', 'Tinderbox', 'Adventuring Gear', '5 sp', '1 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This small container holds flint, fire steel, and tinder (usually dry cloth soaked in light oil) used to kindle a fire. Using it to light a torch--or anything else with abundant, exposed fuel--takes an action.\nLighting any other fire takes 1 minute.'),
('tinkers-tools', 'Tinker''s Tools', 'Tools', '50 gp', '10 lb', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'These special tools include the items needed to pursue a craft or trade. The table shows examples of the most common types of tools, each providing items related to a single craft. Proficiency with a set of artisan''s tools lets you add your proficiency bonus to any ability checks you make using the tools in your craft. Each type of artisan''s tools requires a separate proficiency.'),
